{
  "name": "Kick Comet",
  "created": "2026-09-09T20:03:29.847Z",
  "notes": "Every kick launches one shape from the near end and the strip is whatever is still in flight. The trigger is a `threshold` on the bass band, and `hysteresis` at 0.2 is what makes it a beat detector rather than a buzzer -- without it a sustained note re-crosses its own ripple dozens of times a second and the comets never separate.\n\nThe envelope beside it drives nothing visual. It sets the comet's `velocity`, so a hard kick throws a fast one and a soft kick a slow one. Nothing in `SpawnerEmitter` reads velocity after birth, so the value at the instant of the trigger is the one the shape keeps for life -- the envelope is being SAMPLED rather than followed, which is what `ports/05-fireworks` does with a `sample_hold` for the same reason. `drag` 0.9 with zero acceleration means each comet coasts to a stall at `velocity / drag` and hangs there fading, so hard hits reach further and soft ones die near the bottom.\n\nThe chain runs backwards up the detector: the envelope drives `M0.smoothing`, so immediately after a hit the band is smoothed heavily and the detector goes briefly deaf, then sharpens again as the tail decays. That is a gate's hold time, and it stops a snare inside the kick's decay from launching a second comet on top of the first. Ember run for the comets, cobalt for the bed -- the one cold thing on the strip is the thing they travel over.",
